\title{simpexp: Simulate Event Histories from Piecewise Exponential Hazards}
\description{
Simulates single-event, competing-risks and multi-state event histories from hazards that are piecewise constant on a user-supplied time grid. Each transition is specified by a formula for its log-hazard, which may use the time scales and history features that the simulator maintains, so that non-Markov processes can be specified directly. Because the hazards are piecewise constant by construction, waiting times are drawn by exact inversion of the cumulative hazard rather than by numerical approximation.
}
